//RS /// c109 Phase 10: core/stdlib module calls route through the TIR. `math.*`,
//RS /// `Path.join`, and `crypto.sha256` are type-monomorphic (in `core_fixed_sig`),
//RS /// so `calc`/`make_path`/`hash`/`main` are all covered. The call forms
//RS /// (`jet_std_math_*`, `jet_path_join`, `jet_crypto_sha256_typed_impl`) reproduce
//RS /// `emit_core_call` byte-for-byte; here we prove they compile (I2) and run.
//RS /// parity: guard tests/tir_core_and_closures.rs::core_math_path_crypto_calls
