//RS // NOTE: typed regex calls (`re.is_match(.{…}, …)`) route through the TIR and emit
//RS // `jet_std::jet_regex_*` helpers, so regex-only programs build without an FFI bridge.
//RS 
//RS // ===================================================================
//RS // c109 Phase 11: lambdas/closures, fan-out, closure-taking collection
//RS // methods. Each program lives entirely inside the covered subset, so the
//RS // covered function(s) route through the TIR; the assert proves rustc
//RS // accepts the output (I2) and it runs correctly. Byte-parity to the old
//RS // emitter baseline was verified separately across the example suite.
//RS // ===================================================================
//RS 
//RS /// A list `map`/`filter`/`reduce`/`find`/`any`/`all` with expression-body
//RS /// lambdas, plus a captured (Copy) outer local. The closure methods compose a
//RS /// lambda with the builtin method — the whole `run` routes through the TIR.
